@ 15.2.2 - Proto-Eskimo to Greenlandic Iñupiaq
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Swadesh, Morris (1952), “Unaaliq and Proto Eskimo IV: Diachronic Notes”, International Journal of American Linguistics, Vol. 18, No. 3 (Jul., 1952), pp. 166–171
	ə > u / u_
	ə > a / a_
	C:[+long] > C / except when CV_V in UU
	t > s / i_
	ə > i / else
	d͡ʒ > t͡ʃ / “in certain positions” (except for Thule Greenlandic, where d͡ʒ → t͡ʃ and stayed there, apparently)
	t͡ʃ > s / “in certain positions” (except for Thule Greenlandic, where d͡ʒ → t͡ʃ and stayed there, apparently)
	m n ŋ t {{ɣ,ʁ} > {k,q}} / _#
	{k,q}} > p t k n ŋ / _#
	m n ŋ > v t ɣ / _C:[-nasal]
	l̥ > ʁ / _C
	v ʁ > p q / S_
	v ɣ ʁ > p k q / _C (except where C = /l d͡ʒ m n ŋ/)
	{p,v} t {k,ɣ} > m n ŋ / _N
	SS > FF
	Some metathesis in consonant clusters, the conditions of which are not elaborated upon; the given example cited within the text is lʁ > ʁl
	v > ∅ / u_a
	iv > uj / _u
	d͡ʒ > t͡ʃ / i_{u,i}
	əd͡ʒ > i / _{a,u} (except in #U)
